Subject: [PATCH] usb: functionfs: retain string table allocation until cleanup

The T110 source frees the allocation while stringtabs/t/s still point into
it, then writes through those pointers and publishes the freed table.
Android 13 adbd triggers a kernel Oops in functionfs_bind while walking it.
Restore the allocation lifetime used by the pinned Android common 3.4
donor: malformed input frees stringtabs at error_free, successful input
transfers it to ffs->stringtabs and normal ffs cleanup owns the free.

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_fs.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_fs.c
@@ -1883,8 +1883,6 @@
 		t = d->stringtab;
 		s = d->strings;
 		strings = s;
-
-		kfree(d);
 	}
 
 	/* For each language */
